<title>USA: Ingersoll-Rand names vice chairman.</title>
<headline>Ingersoll-Rand names vice chairman.</headline>
<dateline>WOODCLIFF LAKE, N.J. 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ingersoll-Rand Co said on Thursday it named J. Frank Travis to the board of directors and as vice chairman.</p>
<p>The vice chairman post has been vacant for three years, following the retirement of Clyde Folley, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Travis's election to the board increases its size to 11 members, the company said.</p>
<p>Travis is executive vice president of Ingersoll-Rand and chairman of Ingersoll-Rand Canada, the company said.</p>
</text>
